     {"question": "What is the Page Object pattern in Playwright?", "answer": "The Page Object pattern encapsulates page selectors and actions into reusable classes. This keeps tests readable and maintainable by separating 'what to test' from 'how to interact with the UI'."},
     {"question": "Why use data-testid attributes instead of CSS selectors?", "answer": "Test IDs are stable identifiers that don't break when you refactor CSS classes or HTML structure. Use data-testid for interactive elements that tests need to locate reliably."},
     {"question": "How do I test different user roles in E2E tests?", "answer": "Use different bootstrap helpers: bootstrapAuthenticatedUser for basic users, bootstrapOrgWithMembers for owners, and bootstrapOrgMember for regular team members. Each helper logs in as the appropriate role."},
     {"question": "Should each E2E test create its own data?", "answer": "Yes. Each test should be independent and create its own users, organizations, and data using bootstrap helpers. This prevents tests from affecting each other and eliminates flakiness from shared state."},
     {"question": "How do I use vi.hoisted() for mocking in Vitest?", "answer": "vi.hoisted() defines mock functions before module mocking executes, solving hoisting issues. Define mocks with vi.hoisted(), then reference them in vi.mock() calls. This pattern is required for mocking modules that services depend on."},
